From: Ruhan <35257374+RuhanSA079@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radxa-cm3-io: add external HYM8563 RTC on i2c2

Enables i2c2 (unused until now) and adds the board's external HYM8563
RTC on it. Cross-checked against Radxa's own vendor kernel for this
exact board (radxa/kernel, rk3566-radxa-cm3-io.dts on the
linux-6.1-stan-rkr4.1/linux-5.10-gen-rkr3.4/rkr4.1 branches), which
uses this identical i2c2m1_xfer + hym8563@51 setup -- our tree has no
prior i2c2 usage to conflict with it, and CONFIG_RTC_DRV_HYM8563 is
already enabled in our kernel config.

Note: Radxa's vendor tree also disables rk817's internal RTC subnode
(&rk817 { rtc { status = "disabled"; }; };) when the external RTC is
present, to avoid two competing /dev/rtcN devices. Our rk817 node
(from patch 0001) has no such "rtc" child node at all -- it looks like
a downstream-vendor-kernel-only MFD cell that doesn't exist in this
mainline-based driver stack -- so that part isn't portable here. Both
RTCs may end up registered (rtc0/rtc1); pick the right one explicitly
with hwclock -f if that matters.

Verified the full board dtb still compiles and i2c2's pinctrl-0 and
the hym8563 node resolve to real phandles.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-cm3-io.dts | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-cm3-io.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-cm3-io.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-cm3-io.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-cm3-io.dts
@@ -84,6 +84,21 @@
 	};
 };

+&i2c2 {
+	status = "okay";
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&i2c2m1_xfer>;
+
+	hym8563: hym8563@51 {
+		compatible = "haoyu,hym8563";
+		status = "okay";
+		reg = <0x51>;
+		#clock-cells = <0>;
+		clock-frequency = <32768>;
+		clock-output-names = "hym8563";
+	};
+};
+
 &i2s0_8ch {
 	status = "okay";
 };
